  Physics Adjustments for Full-Screen Spread:
  - Reduced central gravity from 0.008 → 0.001 (nodes won't cluster in center)
  - Reduced gravitational constant from -180 → -50 (less pull to center)
  - Increased spring length from 300 → 400 (nodes spread further apart)
  - More stabilization iterations: 300 → 500 (better initial layout)
  - Added edge length of 400px to push nodes apart

  Canvas Improvements:
  - Changed container to absolute inset-0 to fill entire screen
  - Added autoResize: true and explicit width/height 100%
  - Added layout: { improvedLayout: true } for better initial positioning

  New Feature - "Spread Graph" Button:
  - Click to re-run physics simulation if nodes get clustered
  - Temporarily enables physics for 1 second to redistribute nodes
  - Judges can use this to optimize the view

  The graph should now automatically spread across the entire screen width. If nodes still cluster, click the "Spread graph" button to redistribute them. The lower
  central gravity will keep nodes from bunching in the middle.

  Try running npm run dev to see the improved full-screen layout!

